module

public import Mathlib.RingTheory.RingHom.Flat
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.LocalRing.ResidueField.Basic

/-!
# Flat local extensions with prescribed residue field

Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Lemma 10.159.1 (Tag 03C3)
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-flat-local-extension-given-residue-field).
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u v

namespace IsLocalRing

/-- Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Lemma 10.159.1 (Tag 03C3).
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-flat-local-extension-given-residue-field)
Every extension of the residue field is realized by a flat local ring extension whose
maximal ideal is generated by the original maximal ideal, compatibly over the residue field.

Proof (the nine steps of the node):
1. Compose the quotient R → κ with ι : κ → K. Its kernel is the maximal ideal m.
   Consider towers R → A → K with A local, maximal ideal mA, first map flat, and
   second map having kernel mA. A tower surjecting onto K gives the desired result.
2. For a tower with image F and an element α transcendental over F, localize A[T]
   at mA[T]. Evaluation at α has kernel mA[T]; localization has maximal ideal mB
   and residue field F(α). The polynomial ring is free, localization is flat, and
   their composite is flat [lem-weil-pbc-localization-flat,
   lem-weil-pbc-projective-module-flat, lem-weil-pbc-flat-ring-map-comp].
3. For α algebraic over F, lift its monic minimal polynomial to f ∈ A[T] and take
   B = A[T]/(f). The monic quotient is free, hence flat. Evaluation has kernel mB
   and image F(α). Finiteness over A puts mB in every maximal ideal; since B/mB
   is a field, B is local [lem-weil-pbc-monic-quotient-free,
   lem-weil-pbc-simple-algebraic-extension-power-basis,
   lem-weil-pbc-finite-algebra-local-radical].
4. Composing either extension with R → A produces a tower with image F(α), with
   compatible maps from R and to K [lem-weil-pbc-flat-ring-map-comp].
5. A nonempty chain of compatible towers has a ring colimit. Every element comes
   from a stage. Elements with nonzero image in K are units; elements with zero
   image lie in m times the colimit. Thus the colimit is local with maximal ideal
   m times the colimit, and image the union of the images
   [lem-weil-pbc-filtered-colimit-algebras-elementwise].
6. The same ring colimit is a module colimit: define a compatible linear map on
   stage representatives; equality at a later stage makes it well defined.
   Filtered colimits of flat modules are flat, so this is again a tower
   [lem-weil-pbc-filtered-colimit-rings-zero,
   lem-weil-pbc-filtered-colimit-flat-modules, def-weil-pbc-flat-ring-map].
7. Well-order K. Let K(x) be generated by the image of κ and the elements ≤ x,
   and K(<x) by those < x. Then K(x) = K(<x)(x). The latter is the union of the
   preceding K(y) when the preceding set is nonempty, and is the image of κ
   otherwise [lem-weil-pbc-well-ordering-theorem, def-weil-simple-field-extension].
8. By transfinite recursion take the colimit of preceding towers (R itself in
   the empty case), then adjoin x by steps 2–4. Induction verifies compatibility
   and image K(x) [lem-weil-pbc-transfinite-recursion].
9. Take the colimit over all x. Its image is K, since x belongs to K(x). Steps
   1, 5 and 6 give flatness, locality, equality of maximal ideals, and the residue
   field isomorphism compatible with ι. -/
theorem exists_flat_local_extension_given_residue_field
    (R : Type u) [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] (K : Type v) [Field K]
    (ι : ResidueField R →+* K) :
    ∃ (S : Type (max u v)) (_ : CommRing S) (_ : IsLocalRing S)
      (φ : R →+* S) (_ : IsLocalHom φ),
      φ.Flat ∧ (maximalIdeal R).map φ = maximalIdeal S ∧
      ∃ e : ResidueField S ≃+* K, e.toRingHom.comp (ResidueField.map φ) = ι := by
  sorry

end IsLocalRing
